  "text": "Recipe: Quinoa Chana Dhokla\nCreator: Kusum Dhairyawan\nCategory: Main Dish\nIngredients: cilantro leaves, mint leaves, curry leaves, green chillies, ginger, garlic cloves, toasted sesame seeds, roasted peanuts, lemon juice, green mango, amla, date, water, quinoa, chana dal, spinach, amaranth leaves, turmeric powder, black pepper, hing (asafetida), lime\nCooking methods: blend, soak, grind, steam\nInstructions: GREEN CHUTNEY:\nBlend together 1/2 bunch cilantro leaves, 1 handful of mint leaves, 7-8 curry leaves, 2-3 green chillies, 1 inch piece ginger, 2-3 garlic cloves (optional), 1 Tbsp toasted sesame seeds, 1 Tbsp roasted peanuts, 1/2 lemon juice (or sour fruit like green mango or amla), 1 date for sweetness & some water into a smooth chutney.\n\nBATTER:\nSoak 1/2 cup quinoa & 1/2 cup chana dal in water for 5-6 hours.\nAdd 2 small green chillies, 8-9 curry leaves & 1 inch ginger. Grind to a paste. Let the batter sit overnight or 7-8 hours for fermentation.\nAdd these to the batter & mix thoroughly: a handful of spinach (finely chopped), a handful of amaranth leaves (finely chopped), a handful of cilantro (finely chopped), 1/2 tsp turmeric powder, a pinch of black pepper, a pinch of hing (asafetida), juice of 1/2 lime.\n\nSTEAMING:\nCut parchment paper (or wet cheese cloth) to the shape of a big thali (steel plate). Place it on the steel plate, then pour batter into the plate.\nAdd 2 cups of water in one big wok. Place a ring inside the wok. Let the water boil. Once water starts to boil, place the steel plate with batter over the ring (without submerging the batter in water). Cover the wok with the lid. Let the batter steam at medium high heat for 20 mins until we see the batter leaving the side of the plate.\nRemove the lid. Let the dhokla plate cool completely. Cut into squares for serving. Remove parchment paper.\nNotes: This recipe includes sub-recipes for Green Chutney and Batter. Batter requires overnight or 7-8 hours for fermentation.",
